# Prometheus plugin manager

When the user wants to detect installed AI agent CLIs, browse/install/audit/remove
agent plugins or skills, or check the security verdict of a plugin, use the
`prometheus_*` MCP tools (from the `prometheus` server).

- Detect agents: `prometheus_scan`, `prometheus_superscan`
- Browse: `prometheus_list`, `prometheus_info`, `prometheus_where`, `prometheus_matrix`
- Audit before installing: `prometheus_audit`
- Install/remove: `prometheus_install` / `prometheus_uninstall` — ALWAYS call with
  `dryRun: true` first and show the user the gate verdict + events before a real run.
- Toggle: `prometheus_enable` / `prometheus_disable`

Never set `yes: true` on an install unless the user has explicitly approved the
findings. A `blocked` install event means the nemesis gate refused it.
